{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "label": "Cache-Interface", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der opportunistische Key/Value-Cache des Frameworks: sieben Operationen decken ~95 % der realen F\u00e4lle ab, keine Pattern-Scans, kein Pub/Sub."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_opportunistic_semantics", "label": "Opportunistische Semantik", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Caches sind per Design verlustbehaftet: ein None hei\u00dft \"nicht gecacht\", und der Aufrufer f\u00e4llt auf die Quelle der Wahrheit zur\u00fcck. Implementierungen liefern bei transienten Fehlern Defaults zur\u00fcck statt zu werfen; Missbrauch wirft."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_three_backends", "label": "Drei Backends", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_setifabsent", "label": "setIfAbsent", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Atomarit\u00e4t ist eine Garantie, kein Best Effort: jedes Backend bildet das auf ein einzelnes natives Compare-and-Set ab. ttlMs gilt nur f\u00fcr den Schreibvorgang, der gewinnt, eine Retry-Schleife kann also nie fremden Besitz verl\u00e4ngern."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_incr", "label": "incr", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_acquirelock", "label": "acquireLock", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Schreibt ein zuf\u00e4lliges 128-Bit-Token und l\u00f6scht den Key nur, wenn das Token noch dort steht; die naive Variante \u2014 cache.delete im finally \u2014 wirft den neuen Besitzer raus, sobald ein Halter seine TTL \u00fcberzieht. ttlMs ist Pflicht, weil Ablauf der Weg zur\u00fcck ist, wenn ein Halter abst\u00fcrzt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_bulk_operations", "label": "Bulk-Operationen (mget/mset)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Round-Trip-Optimierung, entscheidend f\u00fcr die Hydratation geteilter Entit\u00e4ten nach einem Sharding-Rebalance."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_no_distributed_consensus", "label": "Kein Lock mit verteiltem Konsens", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Das Compare-and-Delete in release() ist ein get gefolgt von einem delete, kein atomarer Schritt \u2014 die Cache-Oberfl\u00e4che hat keins, und ein Redis-Lua-Skript h\u00e4tte kein Memcached-\u00c4quivalent. Das Restfenster ist schmal, aber nicht null."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_eviction_loses_locks", "label": "Eviction ist der andere Weg, auf dem ein Lock verschwindet", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anders als der Ablauf braucht sie keinen Absturz und respektiert keine Frist; ein false von release() hat damit zwei Ursachen, und nichts am R\u00fcckgabewert sagt dir, welche."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_opportunistic_semantics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_three_backends", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_setifabsent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_incr", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_setifabsent", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_acquirelock", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/cache/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_cache_interface", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_cache_overview_bulk_operations", "relation": "refer